<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Built 2026-08-29, alongside moving com.healthos.morning.plist earlier:
  Francisco wanted the morning readiness/sleep picture ready before an
  8:15am ride-planning decision, and also wanted same-day activities
  (a midday bike ride, an evening BJJ session) and same-day Renpho weigh-ins
  to show up without asking. One early morning run can't see either of
  those, since they haven't happened yet when it fires.

  Runs scripts/quiet_sync.sh (sync + recompute derived metrics + a wellness-
  logging check -- no briefing, no notification unless something's actually
  wrong or missing) once in the evening, so tomorrow's early morning
  briefing already has a complete picture of today, and today's weight
  shows up same-day rather than
  needing a manual sync.

  Not "sync more often" -- Garmin's own wellness data only updates a
  handful of times a day at most (overnight sleep/HRV computed once,
  activities appear once uploaded); polling every few minutes would add
  nothing but overhead. Two well-timed passes (this evening one +
  com.healthos.morning's early one) cover everything asked for.

  21:30 Europe/Madrid is a default, not a measured one -- same spirit as
  com.healthos.morning's own history (07:00 -> 10:00 -> back earlier again
  for this exact reason). Adjust Hour/Minute below and reload if a
  different time fits better (e.g. right before bed, so a late-evening
  session still gets caught).

  Setup:
      cp launchd/com.healthos.quicksync.plist ~/Library/LaunchAgents/
      launchctl load ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.healthos.quicksync.plist

  Verify / run now / remove: same commands as com.healthos.morning.plist,
  substituting this Label (com.healthos.quicksync).

  Output: data/logs/quiet_sync.log.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.healthos.quicksync</string>

    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/bin/bash</string>
        <string>/Users/franciscogostscagliarini/fitness man/scripts/quiet_sync.sh</string>
    </array>

    <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
    <string>/Users/franciscogostscagliarini/fitness man</string>

    <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
    <dict>
        <key>Hour</key>
        <integer>21</integer>
        <key>Minute</key>
        <integer>30</integer>
    </dict>

    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>/Users/franciscogostscagliarini/fitness man/data/logs/launchd_quicksync_stdout.log</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>/Users/franciscogostscagliarini/fitness man/data/logs/launchd_quicksync_stderr.log</string>

    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <false/>
</dict>
</plist>
